# =============================================================================
# Neptune — per-developer overrides (COPY to .developer.env; gitignored)
# =============================================================================
#   cp .developer.env.template .developer.env
#
# .developer.env is layered ON TOP of the committed .env (later wins), and is
# gitignored so your real secrets never get committed. Only set the keys you
# actually need to override — everything else falls through to .env.
#
# Precedence (later wins):
#   appsettings.json -> appsecrets.json -> Key Vault -> .env -> .developer.env
# so anything you set here also wins over a Key Vault value for local work.
# =============================================================================

# --- Azure Key Vault ---
# ON by default (.env sets KeyVaultName=neptune-keyvault-dev; needs one
# `make auth`). Uncomment the empty override to run with no Azure dependency:
#KeyVaultName=

# --- Optional local overrides baked into appsecrets.json by post-create.sh ---
# Leave unset to keep the safe placeholders. Set to test email/AI/storage
# locally without the dev Key Vault.
#SENDGRID_API_KEY=<your-sendgrid-key>
#AZURE_BLOB_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING=<your-dev-blob-connection-string>
# No Anthropic key here: local AI extraction runs through your Claude CLI login (NPT-1133).
# On an ESA laptop (Cato TLS inspection) the CLI can't reach platform.claude.com until it trusts
# the Cato root. Export it to docker-compose/corp-root.crt (see CLAUDE.md), then uncomment:
#NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/workspace/docker-compose/corp-root.crt
# A paid `Neptune.Eval run --api` reads only EvalAnthropicApiKey, passed for that run
# (`EvalAnthropicApiKey=... dotnet run ...`). It spends real credits: agree a budget first.
